  "label": {
    "en": [
      "An old Russian postal card with pre-printed red text and imperial double‑headed eagle emblem on the left. It has a red imprinted stamp at the top right and several circular black postmarks. The card is filled with handwritten cursive text in Russian, addressed to St. Petersburg. The overall style is that of an early 20th‑century Imperial Russian postal stationery card."
